hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"165","We are Muhammad bin Yahya, we are Abu Al-Walid, we are Ikrimah bin Ammar, we are Shaddad bin Abdullah Abu Ammar, and he had caught up with a group of The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Abu Umamah said: Amr ibn Anbasa told us, so he mentioned the hadith in its length describing his conversion to Islam, and he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about ablution. He mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: “Then he should wash his feet up to the ankles, as God commanded him. Unless the sins of his feet come out from the tips of his toes with the water.”"
